# This file is generated from ros-distro-template (template/.github/ISSUE_TEMPLATE/3-robostack-bot.yml.jinja).
# If you change it here, upstream the change: comment `@robostack-bot upstream-to-template` on your PR.

name: robostack-bot command
description: Ask robostack-bot to run a maintenance task (maintainers only)
title: "robostack-bot: "
labels: ["robostack-bot"]
body:
  - type: markdown
    attributes:
      value: |
        robostack-bot picks up this issue, runs the command, replies with the result
        and closes the issue. Commands that change files open (or update) a pull
        request on a `bot/<command>` branch. Only owners, members and collaborators
        can run commands; for everyone else the issue is ignored.

        You can also comment `@robostack-bot <command>` on any issue or pull request.

        | command | what it does |
        |---|---|
        | `update-from-template` | Update this repository to the latest version of the shared template ([ros-distro-template]([= template_url =])): runs `copier update`, then `pixi lock`; when the shared pinning changed it also re-renders `conda_build_config.yaml` and runs `check-deps`. Opens a PR. |
        | `update-rosdistro-snapshot` | Refresh `rosdistro_snapshot.yaml` to the latest rosdistro release (`pixi run create_snapshot`). Opens a PR listing the version bumps. Also runs weekly. |
        | `find-stale-packages` | List packages on the channel that were built against pins that no longer match (`check_dependency_compat.py --stale`), with the `pkg_additional_info.yaml` build-number snippet to rebuild them. Replies only. |
        | `check-template-drift` | List template-owned files that were edited by hand in this repository (they would be overwritten by the next template update). Replies only; also runs on every PR. |
        | `upstream-to-template` | Move those hand edits into the template: opens a PR in [= template_repo =], so every distribution gets them. |

        The conda-forge pinning (`vinca_pinning.yaml`) is shared by all distributions and
        updated in the template repository; it arrives here with the next `update-from-template` PR.
  - type: dropdown
    id: command
    attributes:
      label: Command
      options:
        - update-from-template
        - update-rosdistro-snapshot
        - find-stale-packages
        - check-template-drift
        - upstream-to-template
    validations:
      required: true
  - type: textarea
    id: notes
    attributes:
      label: Notes
      description: Optional context (not read by the bot).
